WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.080
Raj: Each exit says watchdog timeout. Systemd stopped the process after missing its heartbeat.

2
00:00:07.080 --> 00:00:12.384
Lukas: Do we know why the heartbeat stopped? That's different from knowing who stopped it.

3
00:00:12.384 --> 00:00:20.472
Anika: Not yet. Export calls slowed around those times. We don't know if they blocked the heartbeat.

4
00:00:20.472 --> 00:00:27.048
Priya: Just to confirm, nothing got OOM-killed, right? We checked more than the exit status?

5
00:00:27.048 --> 00:00:34.536
Hannah: Yes, the kernel log has no matching OOM event. Available memory stayed healthy.

6
00:00:34.536 --> 00:00:41.184
Raj: No memory pressure in the host charts either. We can rule that out for these exits.

7
00:00:41.184 --> 00:00:47.064
Lukas: And disk writes? The last log incident makes that worth checking, not assuming.

8
00:00:47.064 --> 00:00:53.136
Anika: No sign the disk is filling up. Writes worked, and free space stayed normal.

9
00:00:53.136 --> 00:01:00.168
Hannah: Good. Keep the timeout as a fact, and the blocked-heartbeat idea as a hypothesis.

10
00:01:00.168 --> 00:01:06.600
Priya: Agreed. Don't close off other explanations until we can reproduce the behavior.

